Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Replace per-card GlowBacklight hack with a page-level
 ambient wash
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The per-card light source was a hack repeated per component and exactly
what caused the edge-bleed bug — margins have to be manually tuned per
card size, and it's easy to get wrong. Better fix: give the page itself
real material to diffuse, once, so every glass card on it benefits
automatically via its own backdrop-filter — same principle as the home
page's photo background, but built entirely from CSS radial-gradients
using colors already in the theme (the lavender accent, the existing
ring/blue accent) instead of a new image asset.

Adds .bg-ambient-glow (dark mode only) and wires it into the Library
page background alongside the existing dot-grid. Removes GlowBacklight
and its one usage in product-card.tsx entirely — no longer needed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013tmyB4bNsymQY5xKRXZJD7
---
